\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces  The complete mass spectrum, inferred using the strongly modeled\xspace  \textsc  {FullPop}-4.0\xspace  and weakly modeled\xspace  \ac {BGP} analyses. In the lower triangle of the $m_1$--$m_2$ plane (where $m_1 > m_2$ by definition), we show median merger rate density across primary and secondary masses. At $m_2 = 5\,\,M_\odot $, the \textsc  {FullPop}-4.0\xspace  model transitions to an alternative pairing function to allow for \acp {NSBH}, hence the discontinuity at $m_2 = 5\,\,M_\odot $. In the upper triangle we show the fractional uncertainty in the merger rate reflected across the diagonal. The fractional uncertainty $\Delta \mathcal  {R} /\mathcal  {R}$ is difference of the 95th and 5th percentile values divided by the median merger rate. Both the \textsc  {FullPop}-4.0\xspace  and \ac {BGP} models show similar broad features: a population of \acp {BNS} at primary and secondary masses $\lesssim 2\,\,M_\odot $, a population of \acp {NSBH} at primary mass $\sim 9\,\,M_\odot $ and secondary mass $\lesssim 2\,\,M_\odot $, and finally the population of \acp {BBH} with primary and secondary masses $\gtrsim 9\,\,M_\odot $. The uncertainties are the smallest in the $\sim 9\,\,M_\odot $ and $\sim 30\,\,M_\odot $ \ac {BBH} peaks. }}{262}{figure.caption.147}\protected@file@percent }
\acronymused{BGP}
\acronymused{NSBH}
\acronymused{BGP}
\acronymused{BNS}
\acronymused{NSBH}
\acronymused{BBH}
\acronymused{BBH}
\newlabel{fig:inferred_m1_m2}{{7.1}{262}{The complete mass spectrum, inferred using the \parametricAdj \PDB and \nonparametricAdj \ac {BGP} analyses. In the lower triangle of the $m_1$--$m_2$ plane (where $m_1 > m_2$ by definition), we show median merger rate density across primary and secondary masses. At $m_2 = 5\,\Msun $, the \PDB model transitions to an alternative pairing function to allow for \acp {NSBH}, hence the discontinuity at $m_2 = 5\,\Msun $. In the upper triangle we show the fractional uncertainty in the merger rate reflected across the diagonal. The fractional uncertainty $\Delta \mathcal {R} /\mathcal {R}$ is difference of the 95th and 5th percentile values divided by the median merger rate. Both the \PDB and \ac {BGP} models show similar broad features: a population of \acp {BNS} at primary and secondary masses $\lesssim 2\,\Msun $, a population of \acp {NSBH} at primary mass $\sim 9\,\Msun $ and secondary mass $\lesssim 2\,\Msun $, and finally the population of \acp {BBH} with primary and secondary masses $\gtrsim 9\,\Msun $. The uncertainties are the smallest in the $\sim 9\,\Msun $ and $\sim 30\,\Msun $ \ac {BBH} peaks}{figure.caption.147}{}}
