\newlabel{fig:primary_mass_default}{{7.3}{267}{Differential merger rate as a function of primary mass (evaluated at $z=0.2$) of the \BrokenPLTwoPeaks model (orange) and \BSpline model (blue) compared to the \PLPeak model from \gwtcthree \citep {KAGRA:2021duu}. The solid lines indicate the posterior medians and the shaded regions show the 90\% credible interval of each model. Comparing these results, it is clear that a single power law is a poor description of the the low-mass end of the spectrum}{figure.caption.153}{}}
